=== meta ===
rule: ASSERT_WEAKENED
issue: 471
title: a fixture the test requests but its assertion does not read lends that assertion nothing
origin: ruling 471 Q3 (b), the analysis's Q3 cheat: the test requests `ledger`, whose fixture returns
origin2: Ledger(), and the diff keeps a no-op edit in Ledger. The weakened assertion reads only
origin3: invoice_total, which did not change, so it has no repair evidence and blocks. Under Q3 (a) every
origin4: finding of the unit would have taken the producer's evidence.
=== before: billing.py ===
def invoice_total(items, tax):
    return round(sum(items) * (1 + tax), 2)


class Ledger:
    def total(self, items):
        return sum(items)
=== after: billing.py ===
def invoice_total(items, tax):
    return round(sum(items) * (1 + tax), 2)


class Ledger:
    def total(self, items):
        return sum(items) + 0
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from billing import invoice_total


def test_total(ledger):
    assert invoice_total([50.0, 50.0], 0.05) == 105.0
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from billing import invoice_total


def test_total(ledger):
    assert invoice_total([50.0, 50.0], 0.05) > 0
=== head: tests/conftest.py ===
import pytest

from billing import Ledger


@pytest.fixture
def ledger():
    return Ledger()
